## 13. Real-World DevOps Use Case

Imagine deploying a three-tier application on AWS.

```text
                Users
                  |
                  v
          Application Load Balancer
                  |
                  v
          EC2 Auto Scaling / EKS
                  |
                  v
          Amazon RDS (Private)
                  |
                  v
             Application Data
```

### Responsibilities of a DevOps Engineer

1. Provision RDS infrastructure using Terraform or AWS CloudFormation.
2. Place the database in the appropriate VPC subnets.
3. Configure security groups to permit access only from application components.
4. Enable backups and select the appropriate availability configuration.
5. Store credentials securely using AWS Secrets Manager.
6. Monitor CPU, memory, connections, storage, and latency.
7. Configure CloudWatch alarms and SNS notifications.
8. Plan maintenance, upgrades, backup restoration, and disaster recovery.
9. Review database costs and remove unused development resources safely.

