## 14. Basic AWS CLI Commands

### Describe RDS Instances

```bash
aws rds describe-db-instances --region eu-north-1
```

### List DB Instance Identifiers and Statuses

```bash
aws rds describe-db-instances \
  --query "DBInstances[*].[DBInstanceIdentifier,DBInstanceStatus,Engine]" \
  --output table \
  --region eu-north-1
```

### Describe Manual DB Snapshots

```bash
aws rds describe-db-snapshots \
  --snapshot-type manual \
  --region eu-north-1
```

### Check a Specific DB Instance

```bash
aws rds describe-db-instances \
  --db-instance-identifier mydb \
  --region eu-north-1
```

Replace `mydb` with your actual DB instance identifier.

These commands require AWS CLI configuration and sufficient IAM permissions. They inspect resources; they do not create a database.

