## 17. Interview Questions

**Q1. What is Amazon RDS?**

Amazon RDS is a managed AWS service that simplifies deploying, operating, backing up, monitoring, and scaling relational databases.

**Q2. What is the difference between Multi-AZ and a read replica?**

Multi-AZ is primarily intended to improve availability through standby or failover capabilities. Read replicas are primarily intended to scale read workloads.

**Q3. What is an RDS endpoint?**

It is the network address used by an application to connect to an RDS database.

**Q4. What is a DB subnet group?**

It is a collection of VPC subnets that RDS uses to place database resources.

**Q5. How do you secure an RDS database?**

Use private networking, restrictive security groups, encryption, TLS, secure credential storage, and least-privilege database permissions.

**Q6. How can you monitor RDS?**

Use CloudWatch metrics and alarms, database logs, and supported database performance monitoring tools.

**Q7. What is point-in-time recovery?**

It allows a supported RDS database to be restored to a specific time within its available recovery window.

**Q8. Can RDS scale?**

Yes. Depending on the engine and configuration, you can scale compute, storage, and read capacity using appropriate RDS features.

**Q9. Why not always use a database on EC2?**

A database on EC2 gives more control but requires more operational responsibility. RDS reduces many routine management tasks.

**Q10. What is Amazon RDS Proxy?**

RDS Proxy is a managed database proxy that can pool and manage connections for supported database engines, helping applications handle connection demand more efficiently.

